  "title": "Bigger numbers",
  "goal": "Follow prices, ages and times up to a hundred and beyond, plus દોઢ and અઢી.",
  "tip": "From 21 to 99 each number has its own word, but there are patterns. 21 to 28 end in -વીસ: એકવીસ, બાવીસ, ત્રેવીસ. A number ending in 9 is \"one short\" of the next ten: ઓગણત્રીસ (29), ઓગણચાળીસ (39). Gujarati also has its own words for fractions: દોઢ is 1½ and અઢી is 2½.",
  "lessons": [
